		{"id":"bef5ec236a6e0e34","type":"text","text":"## Delayed Cord Clamping\n- 5 mins\n- 10 cm 15 cm / cut / 20 cm","x":-293,"y":140,"width":348,"height":139,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e7529fba1bd9e05d","type":"text","text":"## [[Shoulder Dystocia]]\n\n","x":-507,"y":-962,"width":299,"height":50,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"bc62578e59e62c41","type":"text","text":"## External Maneuvers (2 min)\n- [[McRoberts]]\n- [[All Fours]]\n- [[Running Position]]\n- [[McRoberts]] + [[Suprapubic Pressure]]\n\n\n","x":-488,"y":-653,"width":280,"height":272},
		{"id":"a291f7f8d7c93734","type":"text","text":"## Normal : Cephalic \n- Dim Lights and encourage dad to be with mum\n- Encourage Mum to push and reassure\n- Perineum Massage\n- Guarding the Head\n- Gentle Axial Traction\n\n\n","x":-507,"y":-1445,"width":440,"height":212,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f66593b10707f71f","type":"text","text":"### Hx:\n- Name & DOB\n- Weeks Gestation ?\n- Gavidy Pavity ?\n- Prenatal and Antenatal Care?\n- Complications?\n- Do you have an obstetrician? What hospital?\n- Position of the Baby?\n- Fetal Movements?\n- How many babies?\n- Contractions? Length.\n- Dilated take note of cm.\n- Rupture of membranes? Waters breaking?\n- Discuss Active and Passive afterbirth","x":-1860,"y":-1460,"width":420,"height":460,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1738afbad81c1aff","type":"text","text":"## **Pause**\n- Consider environment for birth, ambulance ?\n- SITREP\n- Instruct Secondary to set up a Baby Station","x":-1184,"y":-1449,"width":300,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"764f81d14d5f999c","type":"text","text":"## Baby Station:\n- Insulation on the base with a towel\n- Towels for ramping of the shoulders to access airway\n- Prepare Suction\n- Prepare Towels for drying\n- Booties and beanie\n- Umbilical Cord Clamps and Scissors\n- BVM, Masks Set up O2, PEEP Ready","x":-1184,"y":-948,"width":548,"height":294,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"8cf8ed1a353cac6e","type":"text","text":"## Consider ?\n- Is this a premature delivery ?","x":-823,"y":-1690,"width":316,"height":110,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"c2a45ce17e85934a","type":"text","text":"### Signs of Imminent Birth:\n- Urge to Push\n- Bulging Perineum\n- Contractions <2.5 minutes)\n- Dilated cervix?\n- Visible Fetal parts","x":-1775,"y":-912,"width":250,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b4a36ca698522523","type":"text","text":"# Start of the Simulation","x":-2520,"y":-1460,"width":480,"height":80},
		{"id":"4f8af37a3ad4c559","type":"text","text":"## Identify:\n- [[Turtle Sign]]\n- Inability to Birth shoulders\n- Aim for 4 minute delivery","x":-109,"y":-912,"width":280,"height":172,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"9df41a0af270aae9","type":"text","text":"## Internal Maneuvers (2 min)\n- [[Rubin's II]]\n- (+) [[Cork Screw]]\n- [[Reverse Cork Screw]]\n- [[Posterior Arm Release]]\n\n","x":-109,"y":-653,"width":280,"height":272},
		{"id":"57414c103ccd26cd","type":"text","text":"## Primary Survey:\nDRcABC","x":-2405,"y":-1337,"width":250,"height":108},
		{"id":"5173a82e1c2664c7","type":"text","text":"## Good Cry, Tone, Centrally Pink?\n- Skin / Skin","x":20,"y":-166,"width":250,"height":129,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"11f5635254ee4639","type":"text","text":"## Pause & Examine:\n- Perineal Tears\n- Vaginal Bleeding\n- Basic VSS","x":-258,"y":413,"width":279,"height":165,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f92ff910dad640d4","type":"text","text":"## Delivery of Placenta?","x":-322,"y":740,"width":405,"height":56,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"2a7e28b93aedc721","type":"text","text":"## Deliver:\nButtocks and Legs Unassisted","x":304,"y":-1294,"width":250,"height":114},
		{"id":"a158c0eb8cb9bb84","type":"text","text":"## Pause & Examine:\n- Tone\n- Colour\n- Cry?\n- Grimace?\n- Heart Rate\n- Respiratory Status","x":464,"y":-243,"width":275,"height":243,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"8c8c65fdbfa01597","type":"text","text":"## Nuchal Cord ? ","x":401,"y":-987,"width":238,"height":50,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"9e45b691c45d43f5","type":"text","text":"## Dry, Warm, Stimulate","x":601,"y":-640,"width":237,"height":97,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"8bff7c62de99a775","type":"text","text":"## Passive\n- Facilitate natural production of oxytocin\n- Encourage pushing","x":-25,"y":996,"width":250,"height":164,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"9daac542496bdaf3","type":"text","text":"## Visible ? Perform Turnout","x":761,"y":-992,"width":373,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f84c53ea12f9a037","type":"text","text":"## Active\n- IM Oxytocin\n- Cord Traction\n- Guarding the Uterus","x":-460,"y":1001,"width":250,"height":159,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"2822b22f1e3647ca","type":"text","text":"## Airway \n- Meconium ? SUCTION\n- Mouth -> Nose\n- Sniffing Position","x":985,"y":494,"width":298,"height":159,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"bafa01b4662c573a","type":"text","text":"## [[Neonatal Resuscitation Program (NRP)]]","x":961,"y":325,"width":478,"height":56,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dc7359b7fcb5b63c","type":"text","text":"## Breathing\n- Respiratory Status?","x":985,"y":669,"width":298,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"76d843db0f19d8de","type":"text","text":"## Circulation? \n- Identify Heart Rate ?","x":985,"y":805,"width":298,"height":115,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"8a8427d0943050be","type":"text","text":"## Requires IPPV Clamp and Cut\n- Move baby to baby station\n- SITREP","x":1056,"y":-80,"width":288,"height":160,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cd71a3d2b5bfa8c0","type":"text","text":"## Premature ? < 37W\n- Place Baby in a bag\n- Warm, with beanie and booties\n- Blankets and towels\n- Stimulate","x":1137,"y":-640,"width":358,"height":194,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a6e301d573642bcc","type":"text","text":"## [[Postpartum Hemorrhage (PPH) 🩸]]","x":820,"y":1300,"width":510,"height":70,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"96cda585f2a8d0bb","type":"text","text":"## Managing the Placenta\n- Examine for shape, size, integrity\n- Wrap and place in bag for transport","x":-281,"y":1337,"width":323,"height":193,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"183f1134a14ab802","type":"text","text":" - [[Oxygen]]\n - [[Sodium Chloride 0.9%]] - Bilateral Access\n - [[Tranexamic Acid (TXA)]]\n - [[Oxytocin]]\n - [[Fundal Massage]] (following delivery of afterbirth)\n \n\n","x":882,"y":1408,"width":448,"height":178},
		{"id":"5401b94c6c2734e7","type":"text","text":"## Blood Loss > 500 mls ?\n- SITREP (HARU)","x":309,"y":1558,"width":320,"height":125,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"2c779f4634d98981","type":"text","text":"## Assess:\n- Estimate Blood Loss\n- **TONE** – of the fundus ?Recheck in 5 minutes. Urinate.\n- **TRAUMA** - Visible or in Hx?\n- **TISSUE** – Placenta + vessels + membranes are intact?\n- **THROMBIN** – no history of clotting disorders, blood appears to clot, medication history.\n","x":-362,"y":1620,"width":486,"height":251,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"6c4f998b39ac6678","type":"text","text":"**HARU:**\n- Packed Red Blood Cells (1 unit to 2.2 mmol calcium gluconate)\n- Extended Life Plasma (1 unit to 2.2 mmol calcium gluconate)\n- Human Fibrinogen\n\n","x":882,"y":1711,"width":501,"height":179},
		{"id":"7e04926797aaeeb0","type":"text","text":"Arms Released ? ","x":833,"y":-1247,"width":161,"height":67},
		{"id":"5c5df7624843ca68","type":"text","text":"## Consider\n- Allows birth to shoulders unassisted \n- Consider: flexing legs to deliver if position is appropriate","x":639,"y":-1509,"width":303,"height":215},
		{"id":"588e9787cb059ada","type":"text","text":"## Identify:\n- Fetal Buttocks, Hands off!\n- Signs of Cord prolapse? Move cord to perineum ","x":297,"y":-1507,"width":263,"height":187,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"328ebc5f4cf4f71f","type":"text","text":" [[Mauriceau-Smellie-Viet]] - J Shape\n","x":1134,"y":-1413,"width":219,"height":93},
		{"id":"506120d12b19a893","type":"text","text":"## Maneuvers \n- [[Lovesetts maneuver]]\n-  [[Mauriceau-Smellie-Viet]] - J Shape\n","x":1020,"y":-1580,"width":333,"height":140},
